# Required for production — the CRM endpoint leads POST to.
# Until set, /api/lead logs non-PII lead context and returns ok so the form works in dev.
CURBIO_CRM_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional — sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` if present.
CURBIO_CRM_API_KEY=

# Optional — CookieYes site ID (CookieYes dashboard → the sell.curbio.com
# site entry → "Custom-coded site" install snippet — the ID is the path
# segment in that snippet's script src, e.g. .../client_data/<ID>/script.js).
# Renders the consent banner and enables CookieYes's own GPC handling. Absent
# in any environment (dev or prod) = no banner; see lib/consent.ts for how
# the rest of the app behaves with no banner ever having run (CONSENT_DEFAULT).
NEXT_PUBLIC_COOKIEYES_ID=

# Optional — Upstash Redis (Vercel Marketplace integration, installed with
# custom prefix "UPSTASH_REDIS_REST" — hence the doubled "REST" below; these
# are the two auto-provisioned vars for the read-write REST API, not the
# sibling _KV_URL/_REDIS_URL (different protocols) or _READ_ONLY_TOKEN).
# When set, every valid lead is durably persisted (LPUSH leads:v1, capped at
# 5000) BEFORE the visitor gets ok:true, and its delivery outcome is recorded
# afterwards in the leads:delivery:v1 hash, keyed by the lead's leadId.
# Absent = dev mode: log-and-continue, no persistence. There is deliberately NO rate limit on /api/lead — see the
# header comment in app/api/lead/route.ts before adding any submission guard.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_KV_REST_API_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Optional — PostHog project API key (PostHog → Project Settings → Project API
# key). Absent = PostHog no-ops entirely, in every environment, with no crash.
# PostHog is consent-gated like Clarity, NOT like GA4: it has no cookieless
# mode, so it is never initialised until analytics consent is true and opts out
# if consent is withdrawn. See lib/posthog.ts and lib/consent.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Optional — defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com. Set for EU or self-hosted.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# ── /admin authentication ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accounts live in Redis (lib/adminAuth.ts) — people sign up at /admin/signup
# and choose their own password. There is no per-person env var. The owner
# allowlist (who auto-approves on first signup) is in config/adminAccess.ts,
# in version control, since an email address isn't a secret.
#
# The one secret still needed: signs the session cookie. Not tied to any
# individual's credentials — rotating it just signs everyone out.
# Generate: python3 -c "import secrets;print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ── /admin page stats (Vercel Web Analytics) ─────────────────────────────────
# Read-only traffic numbers for the Pages screen. Absent = every view figure
# renders as an em-dash, honestly, rather than a zero — the screen still works.
#
# The token needs read access to the project's analytics only; nothing in the
# admin surface writes anywhere. Create at Vercel → Account Settings → Tokens,
# scoped to the `curbio` team.
#
# TEAM_ID and PROJECT_ID are NOT secrets — they are the same values in
# .vercel/project.json (which is gitignored, so see DECISIONS.md → "Vercel
# project lives under the `curbio` team" if they go missing again).
#
# API notes that will cost you a day if you get them wrong — the params fail
# SILENTLY with a 200 and a plausible wrong answer. See lib/vercelAnalytics.ts:
#   • date params are `since`/`until`, NOT `from`/`to`
#   • the grouping param is `by`, NOT `groupBy`
VERCEL_API_TOKEN=
VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=
